    </content>
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001"><term>adolescence</term><meaning>transition period of physical, cognitive, social, and emotional growth and development of an individual from childhood to adulthood</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00002"><term>amygdala</term><meaning>brain structure responsible for emotional processes</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00003"><term>circadian rhythm</term><meaning>individual’s biologically based pattern of physiological events that occur on a daily cycle</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00004"><term>hippocampus</term><meaning>brain structure responsible for memory formation</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00005"><term>hypothalamus</term><meaning>brain structure responsible for hormonal production and control center</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00008"><term>invincibility fable</term><meaning>feature of the personal fable where adolescents believe that they cannot be harmed or defeated</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00006"><term>limbic system</term><meaning>set of brain structures that develop over the course of adolescence in terms of their primary functionality as well as their connections and coordination with other areas of the brain</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00007"><term>thalamus</term><meaning>brain structure responsible for sensory integration and relay</meaning></definition>
    </glossary>    
    </document>